dType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"860f9140834af1f0601020a82e99cd62e3224b1361726c49740d57cc2aee6d1e","event_uuid":"ad31804c-1c19-4d7e-8f33-e22e0de62b75","position":{"commit_sha":"e70e4915f5bdc12c862cbdea6a3ddbc85e4e5aba","position":"1786123688455251001-ad31804c-1c19-4d7e-8f33-e22e0de62b75"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3fc656990d3945f3d2d180528aab46ebbe43c069144a27ec84da83461a1b705e","event_uuid":"5702a9c8-b7dd-4b2f-adc0-e8dcd8eaa056","position":{"commit_sha":"e70e4915f5bdc12c862cbdea6a3ddbc85e4e5aba","position":"1786123689150206001-5702a9c8-b7dd-4b2f-adc0-e8dcd8eaa056"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786054147160893001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a4b915b9-24f9-4d30-adc7-96fe785ac72b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ae96-f114-5363-4d57"},{"link_uuid":"836c44b5-c1d0-434f-8968-bfa06254a901","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ef38-6a9f-0944-4acc"},{"link_uuid":"937a9a5b-53fb-44e3-827d-8babede59e6e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"69f6-e5ef-99f0-4eec"}],"description":"`.github/complexity-baseline.json` is a shrink-only *gate* protecting a freely-growable *baseline*,\nand unlike `.github/module-size-limit.txt` it has **no CI lock at all**\n(`grep 'complexity-baseline' .github/workflows/` returns zero hits).\n\n## Two distinct defects\n\n**1. No lock.** The module-size limit is locked against `main` in\n`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:363-373`: CI fetches `main`, compares the limit value, and\nhard-errors on any change, so raising it requires an administrator override. The complexity baseline\nhas no equivalent — any contributor change to it lands like ordinary code.\n\n**2. The baseline can be GROWN silently.** `tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py` guards the\nschema, sortedness, `ceiling > 15`, `stale == []`, and `len(ceilings) == live`. Those prevent\n*raising* an existing ceiling and prevent stale entries. They do NOT prevent **adding a new entry**:\nwrite a new function at complexity 30, add its baseline entry, and `live` grows with it — count\nmatches, `stale` stays empty, gate green. There is no assertion that the entry count is monotonically\nnon-increasing and no maximum size.\n\nNet effect: the ratchet only ratchets on functions already in the file. New complexity enters freely.\n\n## Do NOT copy the module-size lock's fail-open\n\n`_build-and-test.yml:372-374` — if the `git fetch` of `main` fails, the lock emits\n`::warning::` and skips the comparison. The comment says \"the absolute cap below still applies\",\nwhich is true but misleading: the cap then runs at the **unverified** `$LIMIT` from the current\nbranch. A change raising `800` to `5000` passes on any run where that fetch flakes. The new lock must\nfail CLOSED when it cannot establish the base value, and the module-size lock should be fixed to\nmatch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] CI locks `.github/complexity-baseline.json` against `main`: a change to the file fails the\n      build unless an administrator overrides the gate, matching the module-size limit's posture\n- [ ] The lock FAILS CLOSED when the base value cannot be fetched — no `::warning::`-and-continue\n- [ ] `_build-and-test.yml`'s module-size lock is changed to fail closed for the same reason\n- [ ] A test asserts the baseline entry count is monotonically non-increasing against `main`, so a\n      new high-complexity function cannot be admitted by adding a baseline entry\n- [ ] Adding a new function above the C901 threshold fails CI even when a matching baseline entry is\n      added in the same change\n- [ ] Legitimate baseline SHRINKAGE (a function refactored below its ceiling, entry removed) still\n      passes without an override\n- [ ] The intended posture — who may change the baseline and how — is documented next to the file\n\n## CORRECTION (plan-review BLOCK, criterion G6) — AC1 and AC6 contradicted each other\n\nThe original ACs asked for two incompatible things:\n\n- AC1: lock the file \"matching the module-size limit's posture\" — and that lock errors on ANY diff\n  to the file.\n- AC6: legitimate SHRINKAGE (a function refactored below its ceiling, its entry removed) must still\n  pass WITHOUT an administrator override.\n\nA whole-file equality lock cannot do both: removing an entry IS a change to the file, so it would\nbe rejected. The plan never said how the lock distinguishes a legitimate shrink from an\nillegitimate grow/add. That gap is the defect; resolving it is a prerequisite, not an\nimplementation detail.\n\n**Resolution: the lock is SEMANTIC, not a byte-diff.** `.github/complexity-baseline.json` is\nstructured data, not a scalar like `.github/module-size-limit.txt`, so the two files cannot share\na lock mechanism. The gate parses BOTH the base (`main`) and the branch copy and compares the\n`ceilings` mappings entry by entry:\n\n| change to the baseline | verdict |\n|---|---|\n| an entry is REMOVED | ALLOWED — this is the ratchet working |\n| an existing ceiling is LOWERED | ALLOWED — same |\n| an existing ceiling is RAISED | REJECTED (administrator override required) |\n| a NEW entry is ADDED | REJECTED (administrator override required) — this is the hole today |\n\nThat is what \"shrink-only\" actually means for a mapping, and it is strictly stronger than the\ncurrent `tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py`, which guards schema, sortedness, `ceiling > 15`,\n`stale == []` and `len(ceilings) == live` — none of which prevents ADDING a new entry. Today you\ncan write a function at complexity 30, add its baseline entry, and the count still matches, `stale`\nstays empty, and the gate is green. New complexity enters freely.\n\nNote the module-size limit's byte-equality lock remains correct FOR THAT FILE, because a single\ninteger has no legitimate direction of travel that should pass unreviewed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes the list above)\n\n- [ ] CI compares `.github/complexity-baseline.json` against `main` SEMANTICALLY and fails the\n      build on a RAISED ceiling or an ADDED entry, requiring an administrator override for either\n- [ ] A REMOVED entry or a LOWERED ceiling passes with no override (the ratchet must stay usable)\n- [ ] The lock FAILS CLOSED when the base copy cannot be fetched — no `::warning::`-and-continue\n- [ ] `_build-and-test.yml`'s module-size lock is changed to fail closed for the same reason: today\n      a failed `git fetch` of `main` emits a warning and then runs the cap at the UNVERIFIED\n      `$LIMIT` from the current branch, so a change raising 800 to 5000 passes on any run where\n      that fetch flakes\n- [ ] Adding a new function above the C901 threshold fails CI even when a matching baseline entry\n      is added in the same change\n- [ ] The intended posture — who may change the baseline, in which direction, and how — is\n      documented next to the file\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","ae96-f114-5363-4d57"],["parent","b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181"],["relates_to","69f6-e5ef-99f0-4eec"],["relates_to","ef38-6a9f-0944-4acc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","parent_status_uuid":"ad31804c-1c19-4d7e-8f33-e22e0de62b75","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"47e9-728e-ba93-485e","ticket_type":"task","title":"Lock complexity-baseline.json in CI and make the baseline shrink-only","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["59a1a6a8-c7bc-4198-89bf-590f3c2bf2c8","a4b915b9-24f9-4d30-adc7-96fe785ac72b","7a3f6514-59de-4bfb-857b-447befee63d8","e1a9bd75-fa2e-4a13-a5aa-17785795abcd","63897516-0866-417e-96f1-582fe4371181","d8b188af-4ec8-4efd-9462-9c03da7989d9","b9c5ba76-0126-4713-8b92-d680ef2e95a1","3065d70f-32c0-4977-901f-062b54ec4a79","ad31804c-1c19-4d7e-8f33-e22e0de62b75","5702a9c8-b7dd-4b2f-adc0-e8dcd8eaa056","836c44b5-c1d0-434f-8968-bfa06254a901","937a9a5b-53fb-44e3-827d-8babede59e6e"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786126328060569154,"uuid":"cb255ff9-6a50-411e-84de-bb955bcf71a4"}